### TITLE ###
greets a name
### ARGS ###
World
### STDOUT ###
Hello, World!

### TITLE ###
shouting uppercases the whole line
### ARGS ###
--shout
World
### STDOUT ###
HELLO, WORLD!

### TITLE ###
repeat prints the greeting several times
### ARGS ###
--repeat
3
Ada
### STDOUT ###
Hello, Ada!
Hello, Ada!
Hello, Ada!

### TITLE ###
a dash reads names from stdin
### ARGS ###
-
### STDIN ###
Ada Grace
### STDOUT ###
Hello, Ada!
Hello, Grace!

### TITLE ###
the locale fixture changes the greeting
### FIXTURE ###
french
### ARGS ###
Ada
### STDOUT ###
Bonjour, Ada!

### TITLE ###
an empty name argument is still a name
### DESCRIPTION ###
The quoted form is the only way to write an empty argument; without it a
line-per-item list cannot tell "empty string" from "blank line".
### ARGS ###
""
### STDOUT ###
Hello, !
